    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74fa36ae_631af576",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_bootjars.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-26T12:51:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this should be cached in a field in the boot image config (or its variant sub-config), since all the information is known at config generation time. Having this generic function is much nicer than the previous ad-hoc location construction in getBootImageConfigs(), but I think it should be called once when the config is constructed. There is no reason to recompute the location every time it is used.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "01a7c730fd3d12844401f435c58300cf1c1196e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07db044e_af8c5dd3",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_bootjars.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065473
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-26T13:37:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did that intentionally.\n\nAt the moment the the struct has dozen fields holding paths... all of which are slightly different variations of each other, with trivial differences, and with field names which give little clue of their mutual relationship. I would rather try to reduce the number of such fields.\n\nIn this case .image points to existing physical file, so it is better candidate to be the canonical field.  ImageLocation is trivially-derived and does not actually represent real file, and thus I prefer to recomputed it on-demand, with the comment moved here to explain it.\n\nI am not really worried about the computational cost of stripping the x86 directory from the string. Code clarity should win.",
      "parentUuid": "74fa36ae_631af576",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "01a7c730fd3d12844401f435c58300cf1c1196e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bf7e1c1_bfe9c01c",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_bootjars.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-26T14:27:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, I find it easier to understand if all configuration happens in one place and at the same time (when boot image config is generated). But I may be wrong.\n\n\u003e Code clarity should win.\n\nNot with regard to build systems --- they need to be fast, and appending lists all over Soong doesn\u0027t help. Note that if this was a heavyweight computation, you also had the option to wrap it in Once().",
      "parentUuid": "07db044e_af8c5dd3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "01a7c730fd3d12844401f435c58300cf1c1196e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "558ab057_2fcf038f",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_bootjars.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065473
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-26T17:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would not consider it part of configuration.\n\nIn general, I am biased against \"trivial derived state\" in programming.  It just invites bugs when the state goes out of sync.\n\nI don\u0027t think append is heavy weight enough to worry.  And we are talking about 3 calls vs 1 call here.",
      "parentUuid": "9bf7e1c1_bfe9c01c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "01a7c730fd3d12844401f435c58300cf1c1196e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
